    "description": "+2 Dmg Glock Mag Extension (Dot Matrix Update): FFFTech/FFFTechnology\n\nOh lookie here boyos, ye found a weapon mod that adds +2 dmg spec to yer lead launcher. \nNo doubt this'll help when we raid the Level 9 Dungeon full'a Orcs...\n\nOh wait, this aint a role playing game... \n\nThis is a +2 mag extension for Glock double stack 9x19 NATO caliber mags. The design \nfeatures ridging that wraps around the front and sides of the extension to aid in \nmag retention within one's grasp when unloading/reloading the pistol. The sides of \nextension are thickened for greater durability if/when the mag is dropped onto a \nhard surface. \n\nCompatible with Gen 3-4 Glock magazines. \n\n\nV1.5 Update: Dot Matrix Baseplate Added\n\n\nPrinter Used: Monoprice Maker Select Plus\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 204C \nBed: 54C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .20mm \nStandard Layer Height: .14mm\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 6\nInfill: 36%\nInfill Pattern: Gyroid\nMaterial Flow: 100%\nSupport Material Percentage: 25%\nSupport X/Y Offset: .34mm\n\n(Block supports for the dot matrix in Cura)\n\n\nHardware Needed: \n\n1x Compatible OEM Mag Body (Such as: Gen 3 G17 mag, or a Gen 4 G19 mag)\n\n1x Standard Length Mag Spring\n\n1x Standard OEM Floorplate (For compressing the mag spring when assembling/disassembling)",
